==German==
[[Image:Nickel silver pot.jpg|thumb|ein '''Topf''']]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|topf}}, from {{inh|de|goh|*topf}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*dupp}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*duppaz|t=hollow, bowl}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*dʰewb-|t=deep, hollow}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|dop|t=a little cup, a thimble}}, {{cog|nds|Dopp|t=shell, pod, bowl}}, {{cog|stq|Dop|t=shell, pod, bowl}}, {{cog|en|dop|t=cup in which a diamond is cut}}.

Both in historic sources and modern dialects, the word is almost entirely restricted to [[East Central German]] (generally as {{m|gmw-ecg|Topp}}, in the very south as {{m|gmw-ecg||Topf}}). [[West Central German]] only shows a neuter derivative in {{m+|gmh|düppen}} (whence e.g. {{cog|lb|Dëppen}}). Nevertheless it must have existed in in Old High German as the {{w|a-mutation}} assures inheritance. Beginning with {{w|Martin Luther|Luther's}} Bible it established itself as the general standard term for “pot”.

